+To move a list over from spreadsheets, `importTasks(list, text)` adds many tasks at once. The text holds one
+task per line, as `title;priority;tags`: the priority may be left empty for `normal`, and the tags are
+separated by spaces, as in `Renew the insurance;high;admin money`. Blank lines are skipped. Each line is
+checked on its own, with the same rules as adding a task, so one bad line does not stop the others. The
+result is `{ imported, rejected }`: `imported` counts the tasks added, and `rejected` lists each line that was
+not added as `{ line, reason }`, where `line` counts from 1 and blank lines are counted too. Lines may end in
+`\n` or `\r\n`, as spreadsheet exports do.
